# Project Review & Setup Instructions

## Objective

Before making any code changes, thoroughly review and understand the complete project.

Do NOT immediately start modifying code.

Your first responsibility is to analyze the project architecture, identify the technologies used, understand the application flow, and detect any missing dependencies or configuration issues.

---

# Step 1 — Analyze the Entire Project

Review the complete codebase including:

- Folder structure
- package.json
- tsconfig.json
- vite.config / next.config
- tailwind.config
- eslint configuration
- environment variables
- assets
- routing
- layouts
- reusable components
- API services
- utilities
- hooks
- state management
- contexts
- styling approach

Understand:

- Application architecture
- Folder organization
- Component hierarchy
- Routing flow
- Data flow
- API flow
- Authentication flow
- State management
- UI library
- Build system

---

# Step 2 — Detect Tech Stack

Identify:

- Framework
- React Version
- Next.js Version
- Vite Version
- TypeScript Version
- Tailwind Version
- UI Library
- State Management
- Form Library
- API Library
- Animation Library
- Icon Library

Do not assume versions.

Read package.json.

---

# Step 3 — Install Missing Dependencies

Check for missing packages.

If any dependency is missing:

- mention it
- explain why
- install it only after confirmation

Never install random packages.

---

# Step 4 — Environment Variables

Check whether project requires:

.env

.env.local

.env.development

.env.production

List all required variables.

If missing, report them.

Do NOT invent values.

---

